# Frontend standards

Askesis UI is **Expo + React Native + expo-router**, not Vue and not Tailwind. There are **no `.vue` files** and no NativeWind/Tailwind classes in this repo. If you encounter a Vue/Tailwind suggestion, discard it and follow the conventions below.

## Mobile-first & PWA / web canvas

- Portrait-only product (`app.json` → `orientation: "portrait"`, dark `userInterfaceStyle`).
- Root UI is wrapped in `MobileCanvas` — on web widths **> 430px**, content sits in a centered phone frame (`MOBILE_MAX_WIDTH = 430` in `src/constants/layout.ts`).
- Design for a single phone column first; do not build desktop multi-column dashboards.
- Respect floating tab bar insets: use `FLOATING_NAV_CONTENT_INSET` (via `Screen` or manually) so content clears `FloatingPillTabBar`.
- Touch targets ≥ **44** pt (`TAB_HIT_SIZE`, primary buttons, shop rows).
- Web preview: `npm run web`. Treat it as a phone-canvas PWA-style shell, not a wide marketing site.

## Screen & composition rules

- Tab screens wrap content in `<Screen title subtitle? rightSlot? scroll?>`.
- Keep the brand signal: `Screen` already renders **ASKESIS** via `typography.brand` — do not replace it with generic headers.
- One job per screen section; prefer existing boards (`SectionBoard`, `StarBalanceHero`, `PenaltyPanel`, `RewardsShop`) over new card systems.
- Cards / elevated panels are for **interactive groupings** only (tasks, shop, forms) — use `colors.backgroundElevated` + `colors.border`, matching neighbors.
- Feedback: `expo-haptics` on primary toggles/tabs; confetti via `ConfettiOverlay` for star wins; Reanimated springs where tabs already animate.

## Styling conventions (exact)

- **Only** React Native `StyleSheet.create` co-located in the file (or small shared style helpers). No CSS files, no styled-components, no Tailwind className strings.
- Colors from `src/theme/colors.ts` only:

  | Token | Hex | Use |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | `background` | `#121824` | Base |
  | `backgroundElevated` | `#1A2233` | Panels |
  | `amber` | `#FFBF00` | Brand / CTAs |
  | `cyan` | `#00E5FF` | Secondary accents |
  | `emerald` | `#00E676` | Success / metrics |
  | `crimson` | `#FF1744` | Penalties / danger |
  | `textPrimary` / `textSecondary` / `textDim` | … | Copy hierarchy |

- Typography from `src/theme/typography.ts` / `fonts`:
  - Display / timer / brand → **Press Start 2P** (`fonts.display`, `typography.brand|pixelTitle|pixelTimer`)
  - Body / UI → **DM Sans** (`typography.h1|h2|body|label|metric`)
- `PrimaryButton` tones: `'amber' | 'cyan' | 'emerald' | 'crimson' | 'muted'`.
- Gradients: follow `Screen` / existing `LinearGradient` usage — deep slate variants, not purple/indigo AI-default palettes.
- Avoid flat undecorated full-bleed white/light themes; this product is intentionally dark and high-contrast.

## Component modularity

- Put reusable UI in `src/components/`; keep route files in `app/(tabs)/` thin.
- Prefer composing `Field`, `NativeSlider` / `DurationSlider`, `TaskToggle`, `PrimaryButton` before inventing inputs.
- Forms that persist must call Zustand stores → services; never write storage from a component.
- Imports: match file-local style (today: relative `../../src/...` from `app/`). Do not mass-migrate to `@/` unless the task explicitly includes it.

## Expo Router specifics

- New tabs/screens belong under `app/` with matching `_layout` registration.
- Preserve custom `FloatingPillTabBar` unless the approved blueprint replaces navigation.
- Typed routes are enabled — do not break `expo-router` file conventions.

## Checklist before finishing UI work

- [ ] Looks correct in a ~390–430px wide column
- [ ] Clears floating nav + safe areas
- [ ] Uses theme tokens (no raw hex except when extending `colors.ts`)
- [ ] Uses `StyleSheet.create`
- [ ] `npm run typecheck` passes
